            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use a sector of angle ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{\\pi}{3}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and area ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "200\\text{ m}^2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $x$ metres be the rope length. The corner angle is $60^\\circ=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ radians, so the accessible grass is a sector of area $200\\text{ m}^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12x^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)&=200\\\\x^2&=\\frac{1200}{\\pi}\\\\x&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1200}{\\pi}}\\\\x&=20\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{\\pi}}\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
